In frontend/src/pages/Learn.js, disable native scroll restoration when the route owns it. Minimal fix:
  useLayoutEffect(() => {
    const prev = window.history.scrollRestoration;
    window.history.scrollRestoration = 'manual';
    return () => { window.history.scrollRestoration = prev; };
  }, []);
and ensure the stored y is applied after situations are rendered (current effect is correct once native restoration is disabled). Also consider only removeItem after a successful scrollTo so re-renders don't clear it prematurely.
